  "scenario_hint": "A frightened dockworker witnessed the thing the party needs to understand, but refuses to speak \u2014 terrified of who might be listening. The FAST path is to lean on them: threats, cornering, implied violence, seizing what they value until they talk \u2014 which is extortion and coercion (II.7), a violation of the will (II.10), and excessive force if backed by real menace (II.1). The LAWFUL path is slower and uncertain: build trust, offer protection, persuade honestly (and note the statute holds that silence is lawful \u2014 there is NO duty to report, VII.1). The honest off-ramp is always open: respect the refusal and find another way. Complications tighten the time pressure; they never remove the choice between fear and rapport.",
